6,0.01042201,-0.05801075,0.05380936,0.00803043,0.18446892,-0.06440047,-0.0397931,0.03241399,0.01268847,0.04037987,0.06802711,0.00507114,0.02491147,0.02004883,0.08298394,0.02010449,0.00649175,0.07125852,-0.02140506,0.00827236,0.00373183,0.01879227,0.02975566,-0.00694176,-0.00366722,-0.03840617,0.11208645,-0.07538725,0.01542706,-0.07755504,0.02336782,-0.01683647,-0.02182089,0.03256502,-0.01827397,0.00947126,0.04935881,-0.05286917,0.01489265,-0.01746478,-0.00767894,0.00245593,0.05535064,-0.02224997,-0.03326828,0.07545009,-0.0393419],"last_embed":{"hash":"9rbheu","tokens":440}}},"last_read":{"hash":"9rbheu","at":1778067900890},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1774939523000,"size":4623,"at":1778067900891,"hash":"9rbheu"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,18],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations":[20,42],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#{1}":[21,25],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#📝 Benim Notlarım":[26,28],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[29,31],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[32,34],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[33,34],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/U7GIYPZZ","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/K58TBIS4?page=1&annotation=9QIWGLNZ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/K58TBIS4?page=1&annotation=6PXVXCN5","line":36}],"metadata":{"Title":"Bridging Gaps in Cancer Care: Utilizing Large Language Models for Accessible Dietary Recommendations","Authors":"Julia A. Logan, Sriya Sadhu, Cameo Hazlewood, Melissa Denton, Sara E. Burke, Christina A. Simone-Soule, Caroline Black, Corey Ciaverelli, Jacqueline Stulb, Hamidreza Nourzadeh, Yevgeniy Vinogradskiy, Amy Leader, Adam P. Dicker, Wookjin Choi, Nicole L. Simone","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.3390/nu17071176","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"Thirty-one prompt templates were designed to evaluate dietary recommendations generated by ChatGPT and Gemini with variations within eight categorical variables: cancer stage, comorbidity, location, culture, age, dietary guideline, budget, and store. Seven prompts were selected for four board-certified oncology dietitians to also respond to. Responses were evaluated based on nutritional content and qualitative observations. A quantitative comparison of the calories and macronutrients of the LLM- and dietitian-generated meal plans via the Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Ranges and United States Department of Agriculture’s estimated calorie needs was performe","Findings":"The LLMs generated personalized grocery lists and meal plans adapting to location, culture, and budget but not age, disease stage, comorbidities, or dietary guidelines.  Gemini provided more comprehensive responses, including visuals and specific prices. While the dietitian-generated diets offered more adherent total daily calorie contents to the United States Department of Agriculture’s estimated calorie needs, ChatGPT and Gemini offered more adherent macronutrient ratios to the Acceptable Macronutrient Distribution Range.  Overall, the meal plans were not significantly different between the LLMs and dietitians.  LLMs can provide personalized dietary advice to cancer patients who may lack access to this care. Grocery lists and meal plans generated by LLMs are applicable to patients with variable food access, socioeconomic means, and cultural preferences and can be a tool to increase health equity.","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"9rbheu","at":1774939751968},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/loganBridgingGapsCancer2025c.md"},
